{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-cursor-1b/option-deny-open",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-CURSOR-1",
    "D-CURSOR-1",
    "CUR-PROV",
    "CUR-POP"
  ],
  "description": "Open a second Database db2 on the same file read-write. For each of dbDenyWrite (1) and dbDenyRead (2) with a table-type and then a dynaset recordset A over F in db: while A is open, db2.OpenRecordset F as a dynaset, as a snapshot and as a table-type recordset reading EOF and RecordCount of each; db2.Execute UPDATE F SET N = N WHERE ID = 1 (dbFailOnError); A Edit, assign N 5, Update, Errors; close A, then db2.OpenRecordset F dynaset and db2.Execute the same UPDATE. Asks whether a deny flag of one cursor affects another Database of the same Workspace for each open type and for a statement, and what is released when A closes. The fixture copy is opened read-write.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
